  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Evaluate ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{3}2\\cdot {5}^{n-1}.$",
  "worked_solution": "The sum takes integer values of $n$ from $1$ to $3.$ So, computing the terms for $n=1,2,3$ and then adding them, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{3}2\\cdot {5}^{n-1} & =(2\\cdot {5}^{1-1})+(2\\cdot {5}^{2-1})+(2\\cdot {5}^{3-1}) \\\\  & =(2\\cdot {5}^{0})+(2\\cdot {5}^{1})+(2\\cdot {5}^{2}) \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 1)+(2\\cdot 5)+(2\\cdot 25) \\\\  & =2+10+50 \\\\  & =62.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
